 "issue": 225,
 "issue_title": "Wrong root pick for meniscus + aperture-misses tunnel through system",
 "issue_body": "**Files:** `src/tracer_2d.py:190-194`, `src/tracer_2d.py:508-534`\n\n- Root pick uses only `R_signed` sign (`min(valid) if R>0 else max(valid)`), ignoring whether the ray origin is inside glass. Fails for meniscus (both centers same side) and concave exits. 3D version does it right.\n- `SystemRayTracer` reallocates `LensRayTracer(...)` per ray per element (pure overhead). On `not ray.hit` it sets `terminated=False` and propagates forward unconditionally \u2014 a ray that missed the aperture teleports to the next lens. `ray.hit` is also clobbered per element, `ray.n` left stale.\n\n**Fix:**\n```python\nself._tracers = [LensRayTracer(e.lens, e.position) for e in system.elements]  # hoist\n...\ntracer.trace_ray(ray, propagate_distance=0)\nif not ray.hit or ray.terminated:\n    ray.terminated = True\n    break  # never clear terminated\n```\n",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/pmaasz/openLens/issues/225",
 "pr": 237,
 "pr_title": "fix(tracer-2d): terminate missed rays instead of propagating downstream",
 "pr_body": "Hoist LensRayTracer per element into self._tracers, synced once per public trace call so lens edits between calls are picked up without per-ray allocation.\r\n\r\nA miss or termination now sets terminated=True and breaks; terminated is never cleared so a ray missing an aperture can no longer teleport to the next lens. Add regression tests for miss termination/path bounds and tracer resync after mutation.",
 "fix_commit": "987514f190eb95c164a72b43777e6b2081bf9b91",
